Meta-level displacement, by contrast, creates a *hierarchical* asymmetry. One system operating at the level of object-language, the other at meta-language, generates something akin to the Liar's paradox structure—but here, mutually consistent, mutually illuminating. Like Gödel numbering: the same symbols encoded at two levels, enabling self-reference without contradiction.

